   "tags": "single | Marks +2 / -0.66",
   "html": "<p>An amplifier circuit is shown in the given figure. Assume standard parameters for silicon and&nbsp;given component V<sub>CC</sub> = 12 V, R<sub>C</sub> = 4 k&Omega;, R<sub>b1</sub> = 60 k&Omega;, R<sub>b2</sub> = 30 k&Omega;, R<sub>e</sub> = 3.3 k&Omega; and &beta; = 150. Use&nbsp;standard values like V<sub>BE(on)</sub> = 0.7 V and V<sub>T</sub> = 25 mV. The magnitude of the voltage gain&nbsp;|A<sub>V|</sub> = |V<sub>0</sub>/V<sub>s</sub>|.</p>\n<p><img style=\"width: 100%; height: auto; max-width: 400px;\" src=\"media/e3/e3f7a3ff668b17dbfefd.png\"></p>",
   "options": [
