   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "single | Marks +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>The circuit shown in the figure is an example of</p>\n<p><img style=\"width: 100%; height: auto; max-width: 400px;\" src=\"media/ec/eccb5f82b23cf1e49509.png\"></p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<p>series - shunt feedback</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "<p>shunt - series feedback</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p>shunt - shunt feedback</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "<p>series - series feedback</p>"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "C"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "C",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>We can see that V<sub>0</sub> is voltage across R<sub>L</sub> and feedback element is R<sub>2</sub>. Since feedback element is&nbsp;directly connected to V<sub>0</sub> [voltage across R<sub>L</sub>]. So we sample voltage.&nbsp;Also the feedback element is connected in shunt with signal source at input so we are mixing&nbsp;current.&nbsp;Thus it is shunt - shunt feedback.</p>"
  },
